    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0441" n="343" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg343"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Count Quadt to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial German Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October 20,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In compliance with
                    instructions, I have the honor respectfully to bring to the knowledge of your
                    excellency the following agreement, arrived at by the Imperial Ambassador Count
                    von Hatzfeldt and Lord Salisbury on the 16th instant, by means of an exchange of
                        notes.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d424-f1"/></p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Secretary of State, the renewed assurance of my most distinguished
                    consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Quadt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d424-f1" n="1" xml:id="d424-f1-content">
                <p>English translation of agreement, printed under Great Britain, <ref
